  Gather the ingredients together.

To cook the Yakisoba noodles, bring @water{220%ml} to a boil in a #frying pan{}. Add the @Nissin Yakisoba Japanese Instant Fried Noodles{1} and cook for ~{2-3%minutes} until most of the water evaporates. If you're using a #stainless-steel pan{}, add a little oil to prevent sticking, but for non-stick pans, oil is unnecessary.

Add the seasoning powder to the noodles, stir thoroughly to combine, and continue frying until all the water evaporates completely.

Using #kitchen scissors{}, cut the yakisoba noodles into smaller pieces to make it easier to fill the bread. Then, carefully stuff the cut noodles into the @hot dog buns{4}, ensuring a generous portion for a satisfying bite.

Sprinkle @Aonori{}(dried green laver seaweed) over the yakisoba pan, then place the @Beni shoga{}(pickled red ginger) in the center for added flavor and a vibrant touch.

Carefully place the stuffed yakisoba pan on a #serving plate{}. This dish is perfect for sharing or as a quick snack on the go! Enjoy!